# Every Dockerfile in this repo builds with the repo root as context
# (`context: .` in .kb/deploy.yaml, or an equivalent CI checkout). Without
# this file, that context includes multi-gigabyte directories that no image
# build ever needs — on a long-lived local clone, .claude/worktrees alone
# (full repo duplicates from agent sessions) and node_modules can push the
# context past 15GB, which stalls `docker build` sending it to the daemon.
# Discovered while building e2e/deploy/config-override's fixture image.

# Version control & editor state
.git
.gitignore
.DS_Store

# Agent session worktrees — full repo duplicates, largest contributor.
.claude/worktrees

# Workspace node_modules — huge, never what a runtime image needs directly.
# EXCEPTION: .kb/deploy/**/node_modules is the `pnpm deploy --prod` output
# every service Dockerfile COPYs from — must stay included.
**/node_modules
!.kb/deploy/**/node_modules
!.kb/deploy/**/node_modules/**

# Build output — same story: excluded broadly, except candidate fixture
# manifests and the CI-produced deploy artifacts used by Docker builds.
**/dist
!dist
!dist/**
!e2e/journey/fixtures/*/dist
!e2e/journey/fixtures/*/dist/**
!.kb/deploy/**/dist
!.kb/deploy/**/dist/**
!.kb/bundle/**/dist
!.kb/bundle/**/dist/**

# Runtime/local-only .kb state — never something an image build should see.
**/.kb/database
**/.kb/storage
**/.kb/analytics
**/.kb/logs
**/.kb/tmp
**/.kb/cache
**/.kb/agents
**/.kb/memory

# Test/coverage artifacts
**/coverage
**/*.log
e2e/*/report
e2e/*/test-results
e2e/tests/report
